\ ==== help for words defined in loaded files ====

\ A definition's declared effect and the \ comment lines above it become the
\ word's entry: man answers { :word :effect :summary }, help prints it, and
\ apropos matches the summary. Consecutive \ lines all extend the summary. A
\ definition with no comment above it, or typed at the REPL, has no summary.

"\ the larger of two numbers, as a float
: larger ( a b -- c ) 2dup < if nip else drop then ;

\ the sum of an array of floats,
\ folded left with +
: total ( xs -- total ) 0 ' + reduce ;

: undocumented ( -- n ) 1 ;

\ -- a comment two lines up does not count

: separated ( -- n ) 2 ;" "/tmp/docs-help.telic" write-file
"/tmp/docs-help.telic" load

\ -- man answers a frame built from the declaration and the comment
' larger man frame>array . cr
' total man :summary @ . cr

\ -- help prints it like a reference entry
help larger
help total

\ -- apropos matches the summary of a loaded word and shows its effect
"folded left" apropos

\ -- no comment above the definition: an entry with no summary
' undocumented man . cr
' separated man . cr

\ -- a REPL definition records no location, so it has no entry
\ typed here, not loaded
: at-repl ( n -- n' ) 1+ ;
' at-repl man . cr

\ -- the words still run
3 7 larger . [ 1 2 3 ] total . 5 at-repl . cr
